WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.105
Intelligence coordination depends on source discipline. A source may be internal

00:00:04.105 --> 00:00:04.735
telemetry,

00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:08.910
a public report, a partner tip, a vendor advisory, a fraud record, a case note,

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.430
a sanitized incident summary, or a regulated reporting channel.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:16.020
Different sources have different reliability, credibility, access limits,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.260
and handling rules. Treating all sources as equal leads to poor analysis and damaged

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:20.480
trust.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.455
Provenance records where information came from and how it moved. Analysts should document

00:00:24.455 --> 00:00:26.080
when the information was received,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.915
who provided it or which system produced it, what transformations were performed,

00:00:29.915 --> 00:00:34.170
what limitations apply, and whether any caveats or handling restrictions came with it.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.420
If a source was summarized, redacted, aggregated, normalized,

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.852
or combined with another dataset,

00:00:38.852 --> 00:00:41.850
that transformation should be visible to authorized reviewers.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.980
Source reliability and information credibility are related but separate. A generally

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.060
reliable partner can pass along an unconfirmed observation.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.770
A public report can be accurate on one point and incomplete on another.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.910
Internal telemetry can be precise but limited by logging gaps or retention windows.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.979
Analysts should describe what the source supports, what it does not support,

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:02.470
and how confident they are in the interpretation.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.280
Handling rules control who can see information, how it can be stored,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.800
how long it can be retained, whether it can cross borders, whether it can be quoted,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.960
and whether it can be shared only as a summary.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.630
Some partner information may be usable for internal analysis but not for external

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.450
dissemination.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.550
Some sensitive records may require access controls, markings,

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.350
or legal review. Some details may need to be removed before sharing with a broader

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:22.950
audience.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.895
Respecting handling rules protects accuracy and relationships. A partner that shares a

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:30.795
limited warning may stop sharing if the information is redistributed without permission.

00:01:30.795 --> 00:01:35.205
A privacy team may reject a product that includes identifiers not needed for the decision.

00:01:35.205 --> 00:01:39.110
A regulator or customer may need carefully caveated findings rather than raw working

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:39.540
notes.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.430
Provenance and handling discipline help the team use information responsibly while

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.240
preserving the trust that makes coordination possible.
